 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps a callback so it runs inside the app context. It's the equivalent of Flask's `with_appcontext`.\n\nYou often won't need it. Commands registered with `@app.cli.command()` (`src/tessel/app.py:338`) or `@bundle.cli.command()` (`src/tessel/bundles.py:49`) already get it. Both are `AppGroup` instances, and `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) applies `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n\nUse `needs_app_scope` explicitly only on a plain `click` command that isn't registered under an `AppGroup`.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo`, at `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (`cli.py:333`) finds and imports the app. `needs_app_scope` calls it at `cli.py:397`. `TesselGroup` (`cli.py:531`) is the top-level `tessel` CLI group, and it also calls `load_app()` to list commands.",
